.TH QUADRF-NTSC-TX 1 "September 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-ntsc-tx \- transmit analogue NTSC video
.br
quadrf-ntsc-mod \- NTSC FM modulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-ntsc-tx
.br
.B quadrf-ntsc-mod
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadrf-ntsc-tx
is the Camera Encoder launcher. It programmes the MAX2850 with
.BR quadrf-jtag (1)
and runs the modulator. The default picture is a built-in colour-bar still
on Raceband 5 (5806 MHz). A small identification is burned into the
lower-right corner:
.B CALLSIGN
from
.IR /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf ,
or
.B NOCALL
when that field is unset (the factory default).
.PP
.B quadrf-ntsc-mod
builds composite NTSC (sync, burst, luma and chroma) from a test pattern, a
still image, or a video file, FM-modulates it at 8 times the colour subcarrier,
and writes CS8 IQ to the SoapySDR TX stream. The waveform is meant to be
decoded by
.BR quadrf-ntsc-demod .
.PP
Environment for the launcher:
.BR QUADRF_NTSC_TX_INPUT
(image or MP4 path),
.BR QUADRF_NTSC_TX_PATTERN
(bars, smpte, grid, checker, white, black, red, green, blue),
.BR QUADRF_NTSC_TX_CH
(R1–R8),
.BR QUADRF_NTSC_TX_GAIN
(0–63; keep at or below 25 for close-range tests).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --pattern " name"
Built-in still (default
.BR bars ).
.TP
.BI --input " path"
Image (looped) or video/MP4. A trailing
.B .ppm
is loaded without ffmpeg. Use
.B --still
to force a video file to a single frame.
.TP
.BI --ch " Rn"
Raceband channel R1–R8 (default R5).
.TP
.BI --gain " n"
TX gain 0–63 (default 20).
.TP
.BI --callsign " id"
Override the burned-in identification. Default is
.B CALLSIGN
from
.IR /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf
(factory default
.BR NOCALL ).
.TP
.BI --duration " s"
Stop after
.I s
seconds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf-ntsc (1),
.BR quadrf-jtag (1)
